Jahshaka patch 0030 — a reflection probe's captured DEPTH was encoded against
the wrong direction on GLSL/Vulkan (and Metal), so every off-centre probe lied
about how far it could see along X and Y.

MEASURED, not argued (lane-probevis, 2026-09-13; RTX 4080S, the probe cube read
back texel by texel through AsyncTextureTicket). A sealed 20 x 5 x 8 room with
a 2 x 1 x 1 probe grid, probes at x = -5 and +5, the mirror surface 2.256 m from
probe 0:

    probe 0, towards the mirror   true 2.256 m   recorded 1.058 m   (47%)
    probe 1, same surface         true 12.21 m   recorded 31.03 m   (254%, saturated)

and, in an asymmetric coloured room (walls at 1.5 m and 4.5 m in X, 2 m in Y,
2 m and 6 m in Z, so every face is a different distance):

    +X  true 4.50  recorded 9.30 (saturated)      -X  true 1.50  recorded 0.49
    +Y  true 2.00  recorded 2.00                  -Y  true 2.00  recorded 2.00   (camera on the Y centre line: no error to see)
    +Z  true 6.00  recorded 6.00                  -Z  true 2.00  recorded 2.00

With this patch every one of those reads its true distance (4.50 / 1.50 / 2.00 /
2.00 / 6.00 / 2.00, and 2.275 m / 12.168 m for the two probes above).

THE CAUSE. `PccDepthCompressor_ps.any` reconstructs each texel's view-space
position from the depth buffer and rotates that direction into the probe's local
space to ask how far the probe's own parallax box is that way (`fApproxDist`,
the divisor the compressed depth is stored against):

	probeToPosDir = mul( p_viewSpaceToProbeLocalSpace, probeToPosDir );

`mul` is `#define mul( x, y ) ((x) * (y))` in the GLSL and Metal wrappers, so
that is `mat3 * vec3`. But Ogre uploads a `Matrix3` ROW BY ROW into the padded
COLUMNS of that mat3 (`GpuProgramParameters::setNamedConstant( const String &,
const Matrix3 & )`, OgreGpuProgramParams.cpp:3208-3224), so in GLSL `M * v`
evaluates the TRANSPOSE and `v * M` is the intended product. Upstream's own Hlms
piece knows this and splits the very same product by syntax
(`Cubemap_piece_all.any`, `toProbeLocalSpace`: `mul( viewSpaceToProbeLocal,
posLS )` for hlsl, `posLS * viewSpaceToProbeLocal` otherwise); the compressor
material, which is a plain low-level material and not an Hlms template, does
not.

WHY IT HID FOR SO LONG. The transpose of a rotation is its inverse, and the two
Z faces' cubemap rotations are their own inverses (identity for +Z, 180 degrees
about Y for -Z), so the Z axis is exactly right either way. The X and Y faces'
rotations are +-90 degrees, and there the inverse MIRRORS the direction — but
the only consumer is `fApproxDist`, the distance from the probe camera to its
own box, which is SYMMETRIC when the camera sits at the box centre. A probe in
the middle of its parallax box therefore records the truth. Every other probe
records `0.5 * fDist / fApproxDist( mirrored direction )`, which is why the
error looks like a random scale factor per face and per probe.

WHAT IT BREAKS, all three of which are Jahshaka pain recorded elsewhere:
  * `PccPerPixelGridPlacement::buildEnd`'s shrink-fit reads those alphas, one
    averaged value per cube face, and reconstructs a box from them — the fit
    that Jahshaka's A2 clamp exists to contain ("shapes reaching +-23.68 in a
    room spanning +-12.25", OgreGi.cpp clampProbeShapesToRegion). With the
    encoding fixed the fitted shapes hug the room: measured, an asymmetric room
    fits to half (3.01, 2.01, 4.02) against a true (3.00, 2.00, 4.00), and every
    probe of a grid agrees on it.
  * `getPccVctBlendWeight` refines the PCC hit with the same compressed depth
    before comparing it against the VCT cone hit (Vct_piece_ps.any), so the
    hybrid's trust window was measured against a mirrored distance.
  * patch 0029's visibility test, which is the consumer that made it visible:
    a probe that thinks it can only see 1 m declares a legitimate mirror
    occluded, which is exactly the "sealed room goes black" failure that parked
    0029 for a day (REFLECTION_PROBE_AUDIT, ledger 130/135).

HLSL IS LEFT EXACTLY AS UPSTREAM SHIPPED IT — AND IS SUSPECTED WRONG FOR THE
SAME REASON. This lane has no D3D11 box, so that path is UNMEASURED and the
patch does not touch it; but the reasoning that would make it safe does not
hold. Ogre compiles HLSL with `D3DCOMPILE_PACK_MATRIX_COLUMN_MAJOR`
(OgreD3D11HLSLProgram.cpp:494, used at :1580) and the Matrix3 upload above has
no transpose anywhere (the transposing path in OgreGpuProgramParams.cpp,
:1109-1122, covers Matrix4 only), so a cbuffer `float3x3` there receives the
same rows-into-columns layout and `mul( m, v )` is most likely the transpose on
D3D11 too. What makes `mul( m, v )` right in the Hlms pieces is that their
matrix is ROW-CONSTRUCTED inside the shader (`buildMidf3x3( row0, row1, row2 )`
from three float4 fetches) rather than uploaded as a matrix at all — a
different thing entirely from this uniform. Recorded in
SPECS/OGRE_UPSTREAM_ISSUES.md; whoever gets a D3D11 target should measure it and
flip the HLSL macro the same way if it reproduces. The patch introduces one
macro, `OGRE_MUL_M3V`, defined per wrapper, and changes no arithmetic anywhere
else.

MEDIA-only (a low-level material's shaders). Studio stages media from the
SOURCE tree, so every tree needs the patch loop / build-ogre.sh rerun; no C++ is
rebuilt by it. A tree that has 0029 without this one renders a black mirror in a
sealed room — the two ship together.

Covered by tests/gi/test_gi_probe_visibility.cpp phase 2 (gi.probe_visibility):
the long-room mirror reads r 1.000 with this patch and r 0.000 without it.
diff --git a/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/Any/PccDepthCompressor_ps.any b/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/Any/PccDepthCompressor_ps.any
index 2efaf1be5..014e64b77 100644
--- a/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/Any/PccDepthCompressor_ps.any
+++ b/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/Any/PccDepthCompressor_ps.any
@@ -30,7 +30,10 @@ INLINE float findIntersectionDistance( float3 reflDirLS, float3 posLS, float3 pr
 	float fDist = length( viewSpacePosition.xyz );
 	float3 probeToPosDir = viewSpacePosition / fDist;
 
-	probeToPosDir = mul( p_viewSpaceToProbeLocalSpace, probeToPosDir );
+	// Jahshaka: the matrix multiply must follow the SYNTAX's convention --
+	// see OGRE_MUL_M3V in each wrapper (upstream's own Hlms piece splits the
+	// same product by syntax: Cubemap_piece_all.any toProbeLocalSpace).
+	probeToPosDir = OGRE_MUL_M3V( p_viewSpaceToProbeLocalSpace, probeToPosDir );
 
 	float fApproxDist = findIntersectionDistance( probeToPosDir, p_cameraPosLS, p_probeShapeHalfSize );
 
diff --git a/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/GLSL/PccDepthCompressor_ps.glsl b/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/GLSL/PccDepthCompressor_ps.glsl
index 7864107b0..a6a55967d 100644
--- a/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/GLSL/PccDepthCompressor_ps.glsl
+++ b/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/GLSL/PccDepthCompressor_ps.glsl
@@ -7,6 +7,9 @@
 #define float3x3 mat3
 
 #define mul( x, y ) ((x) * (y))
+// Ogre uploads a Matrix3 ROW BY ROW into the padded columns of a GLSL mat3, so
+// `M * v` computes the TRANSPOSE and `v * M` is the intended M*v.
+#define OGRE_MUL_M3V( m, v ) ((v) * (m))
 #define INLINE
 
 #ifdef VULKAN
diff --git a/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/HLSL/PccDepthCompressor_ps.hlsl b/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/HLSL/PccDepthCompressor_ps.hlsl
index c40a01f27..46f3cb2cb 100644
--- a/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/HLSL/PccDepthCompressor_ps.hlsl
+++ b/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/HLSL/PccDepthCompressor_ps.hlsl
@@ -1,6 +1,10 @@
 
 #define INLINE
 
+// HLSL keeps mul( matrix, vector ) -- the convention upstream's Hlms pieces
+// already assume for this syntax (Cubemap_piece_all.any toProbeLocalSpace).
+#define OGRE_MUL_M3V( m, v ) mul( (m), (v) )
+
 #define OGRE_Sample( tex, sampler, uv ) tex.Sample( sampler, uv )
 
 struct PS_INPUT
diff --git a/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/Metal/PccDepthCompressor_ps.metal b/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/Metal/PccDepthCompressor_ps.metal
index 9e84c4999..b1b0a70e9 100644
--- a/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/Metal/PccDepthCompressor_ps.metal
+++ b/Samples/Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/Metal/PccDepthCompressor_ps.metal
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@
 using namespace metal;
 
 #define mul( x, y ) ((x) * (y))
+// Same convention as GLSL: Ogre's rows land in the matrix's columns.
+#define OGRE_MUL_M3V( m, v ) ((v) * (m))
 #define INLINE inline
 #define OGRE_Sample( tex, sampler, uv ) tex.sample( sampler, uv )
 
